      "text": [
        " «هُوَ وَاجِبٌ عَلَى كُلِّ مُسْلِمٍ إِلاَّ مَنْ لَمْ يَجِدْ» فَقَالَ لَهُ اَلسَّائِلُ فَمَا تَرَى فِي اَلْعِيَالِ قَالَ «إِنْ شِئْتَ فَعَلْتَ وَ إِنْ شِئْتَ لَمْ تَفْعَلْ وَ أَمَّا أَنْتَ فَلاَ تَدَعْهُ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3044 - It is narrated from Al-ʿAlāʾ ibn al-Fuḍayl, from Abu ʿAbdillah (as), that a man asked him about the sacrifice (udhiyya).\nImam (as) replied: \"It is obligatory upon every Muslim except for one who cannot afford it.\"\nThe questioner then asked: \"What do you say regarding the dependents?\"\nImam (as) said: \"If you wish, you may perform it for them, and if you wish, you may not. However, as for you, do not neglect it.\""
        ]
      }
